 "about_text": "PHASE Gallery is an artist-run exhibition space in the Lincoln Heights/Cypress Park area of Los Angeles, founded in 2022 by artists Ewa Słapa and Brad Howe. The gallery presents an experimental, cross-generational program of solo and group shows spanning painting, sculpture, video, sound, and installation, often accompanied by essays from critics and curators such as Jan Tumlir and Sabrina Tarasoff. Exhibitions have paired historical material, such as a collection of children's drawings by early-childhood researcher Rhoda Kellogg, with work by contemporary Los Angeles-based artists. The gallery also hosts public talks and lectures, including a philosophy lecture by Catherine Malabou, positioning itself as a meeting point for artists, thinkers, and the wider community around emerging and experimental practice.",
